# Frontend (Next.js) environment — template. Copy to .env.local for local dev.
#
# In PRODUCTION none of these are required. The frontend and backend share one
# origin (the host's system Caddy routes /api/* + /health to the backend and
# everything else to this app), so the browser calls the API with RELATIVE paths
# (/api/...). There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL and no absolute backend URL to set.
#
# Container runtime vars (NODE_ENV, PORT=3000, HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0) are provided by
# docker-compose.yml, not from this file.

# Local development WITHOUT Caddy only:
# Turns on a dev-only Next.js rewrite (see next.config.mjs) so /api/* is proxied
# to the running backend. Leave UNSET in production — Caddy does the routing.
# DEV_API_PROXY=http://localhost:8080
